// The stable process exit-code table (E2-M3), the statuses' one home. The
// numbers are part of the public contract that scripts and CI read; they
// never change meaning (Docs/spec/release-policy.md, "Exit-code table").
// Tools/agent/RuntimeGenerators.jet generates the runtime's, the test kit's
// and Core's copies from these rows, and fails on a bare 70 or 101 in an
// exit position anywhere else.

// Everything succeeded.
EXIT_OK: 0
// An unhandled entry error report, or a driver-reported user problem.
EXIT_USER_ERROR: 1
// The command line itself was wrong: unknown command, missing argument, or a
// flag that does not apply.
EXIT_USAGE: 2
// A built program breached or stopped at runtime.
EXIT_RUNTIME_PANIC: 70
// Jet's own compiler defect; never a user-program exit.
EXIT_ICE: 101
